1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,005
Nvidia's CEO just walked out the door.

2
00:00:03,055 --> 00:00:06,667
Jensen Huang has resigned, effective immediately.

3
00:00:06,717 --> 00:00:12,186
He co-founded the company in nineteen ninety three, and ran it for thirty three years.

4
00:00:12,236 --> 00:00:16,201
For now, finance chief Colette Kress is interim CEO.

5
00:00:16,251 --> 00:00:19,917
Harvey Jones becomes the company's first ever board chair.

6
00:00:19,967 --> 00:00:23,025
And the search for a permanent CEO has begun.

7
00:00:23,075 --> 00:00:25,034
Nvidia hasn't said why.

8
00:00:25,084 --> 00:00:31,235
News reports point to a week of pressure, but those details are reported, not confirmed.

9
00:00:31,285 --> 00:00:39,335
Shares fell more than ten percent in early trading, then recovered to about four percent down, according to CNBC.

10
00:00:39,385 --> 00:00:40,833
Oh, hi Muja.

11
00:00:40,883 --> 00:00:42,581
So why does it matter?

12
00:00:42,631 --> 00:00:50,745
Nvidia supplies most of the chips behind advanced AI, and there was no succession plan in place, says TechCrunch.

13
00:00:50,795 --> 00:00:55,271
Third quarter results are still due on Tuesday, November seventeenth.

14
00:00:55,321 --> 00:00:59,190
That call is the first big test for the interim CEO.

15
00:00:59,240 --> 00:01:03,781
My take: hold off on big hardware decisions until after that call.

16
00:01:03,831 --> 00:01:06,185
Full sources are on my blog.
